Subtract one full turn.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}425^{\circ}\\&\equiv425^{\circ}-360^{\circ}\\&\equiv65^{\circ}\end{aligned}$
The two angles point in the same direction.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=10mm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{angleblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[<->,black] (-1.6,0)--(1.6,0);
\draw[<->,black] (0,-1.3)--(0,1.6);
\path (1.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\path (0,1.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[->,angleblue,thick] (0,0)--(65:1.45);
\draw[->,angleblue] (0.55,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=65,radius=0.55];
\path (32.5:0.95) node[text=angleblue] {$65^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
